    "created_at": "2026-11-16T07:19:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-16T07:19:29Z",
    "body": "chromium side: `area { display: none }` has been the UA default since the HTMLAreaElementDisplayNone flag flipped stable, and i just landed https://crrev.com/c/8261073 removing the kill switch, so it's permanent now.\n\n@emilio is right that we're not fully gecko-equivalent, our rule has no `!important` and there's no c++ enforcement, so `area { display: block }` still produces a box,  happy to make it author-un-overridable in blink if the spec goes that way.\n",
